<p>
  <strong>{{ metadata.title }}</strong> is an Eleventy starter that keeps the
  original Tacit feel: minimal HTML, centered content, and typography that does
  the layout work for you without utility classes.
</p>

<pre>&lt;!doctype html&gt;
&lt;html&gt;
  &lt;head&gt;
    &lt;link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/tacit.css"&gt;
  &lt;/head&gt;
&lt;/html&gt;</pre>

<p>
  The layout on this starter now follows the same shell as the upstream demo:
  a logo row, a simple navigation row, a framed article body, and a quiet
  footer. The logo uses the official 11ty artwork instead of the upstream Tacit
  bird mark.
</p>

<p>
  You can keep writing plain HTML and Markdown for pages, posts, forms, lists,
  tables, and figures. Tacit still styles the native elements directly, so the
  markup stays small.
</p>

<h2>Latest posts</h2>
<ul>
  {% for post in collections.posts | slice(0,3) %}
    <li>
      <strong><a href="{{ post.url }}">{{ post.data.title }}</a></strong><br>
      <small>{{ post.date | date("LLL d, yyyy") }}</small><br>
      {{ post.data.description or post.templateContent | striptags | truncate(140) }}
    </li>
  {% else %}
    <li>No posts yet.</li>
  {% endfor %}
</ul>

<h2>Starter pages</h2>
<p>
  Browse the <a href="/about/">about page</a>, submit the <a href="/contact/">contact form</a>,
  or read the <a href="/blog/">blog index</a> to see how the shared layout holds up
  across the rest of the site.
</p>
